[h1]OpenZone Research[/h1]
Research points and a technology tree for OpenZone servers. Raw finds go into a packer and come out as a sample of its line, an analyzer turns the sample into a carrier, the carrier is handed in at a faction terminal, and the faction's pool is spent on its own tree, instantly or as a timed project. Every rule, point type, station and tree node is the administrator's JSON. Part of the OpenZone series, made for the whole Ukrainian DayZ community.

[b]What you get[/b]
[list]
[*]Seven lines: biology, anomalies, electronics, loot, trails, ballistics and protection. Each has one sample, one analysis and one carrier, shared by every faction that works the line; the line is also the point type.
[*]Stations: put the input into a station's cargo and press F; the station works by the clock (a restart loses nothing), puts the result into its own cargo and keeps going while input is left.
[*]Rules in JSON: which device takes what, how long, what comes out and with what chance. A packer rule sets the sample's points, the rarity of the input, and its starting purity, 0.7 by default; each module of the line in the packer's three slots adds 0.1 purity and a 10% chance of a second sample. Analyzers and terminals take no modules.
[*]The item carries the numbers, read only by the server: a sample holds its points and its purity, the chance that its analysis succeeds; the carrier keeps the points.
[*]Terminals: an identified carrier shows its line and points; handing it in pays the pool of the faction of whoever hands it in.
[*]The tree: branches per faction, nodes with a cost in line points and materials, instant nodes and timed projects, parents by "all" or "any"; the leader or the holder of the research post spends.
[*]The tree screen: rows laid out by the engine, node icons, the faction's own backdrop and a fog of war over what lies too far ahead.
[*]Static stations from JSON, an example types.xml and two example packs: seven factions in full, and a test stand.
[*]Administration in the OpenZone admin window (VPP): the seven configs in the CONFIG pane, the RESEARCH pane for pools, resets, grants and reloads.
[/list]
[b]Requires[/b] [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1559212036]Community Framework[/url] and [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3798432022]OpenZone Core[/url]. Factions come from [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3798436325]OpenZone Factions[/url]; without it every player belongs to the default owner from the settings.
[b]Companion[/b] [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3804762616]OpenZone Research VPP[/url] (the RESEARCH pane of the admin window).
[b]Source code[/b] [url=https://github.com/OpenZone-DayZ/openzone-research]github.com/OpenZone-DayZ/openzone-research[/url]

[b]Licence, repacking, selling[/b]
You may repack this mod into your server's own pack, keeping the attribution and the same licence. You may not sell it, sublicense it or include it in any paid bundle. Running it on a server that accepts donations, sells cosmetics or priority queue slots is fine. CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 with the additional permission in NOTICE.

